        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.16,
          "end": 307.713,
          "en": "And you see that for all the meals, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.3,
          "end": 313.14,
          "en": "Now, by the way, you might be wondering why here we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.14,
          "end": 317.1,
          "en": "a row, which my MealItemTrait returns in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.1,
          "end": 318.84,
          "en": "inside of another row.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.84,
          "end": 320.289,
          "en": "Normally we would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.289,
          "end": 324.34,
          "en": "and we would need to use Expanded, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 324.34,
          "end": 327.33,
          "en": "Well, here it works without Expanded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.33,
          "end": 331.59,
          "en": "because this row is inside of a column which is inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 331.59,
          "end": 333.115,
          "en": "of this positioned widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 333.115,
          "end": 336.338,
          "en": "which has left and right set to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.338,
          "end": 341.338,
          "en": "Therefore, this positioned widget enforces its child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 341.46,
          "end": 344.67,
          "en": "the container, to take exactly that width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 344.67,
          "end": 347.03,
          "en": "between the left border of this stack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.03,
          "end": 349.803,
          "en": "and the right border of this stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.7,
          "end": 353.79,
          "en": "And therefore we actually have a fixed width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.79,
          "end": 357.51,
          "en": "And this fixed width is passed down from the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 357.51,
          "end": 360.18,
          "en": "to the column and from the column to this row.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 360.18,
          "end": 361.68,
          "en": "So therefore, this row here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.68,
          "end": 364.23,
          "en": "is not unconstrained horizontally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 364.23,
          "end": 367.02,
          "en": "And hence it has no problem with another row being",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 367.02,
          "end": 369.75,
          "en": "inside of it because even though this row here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 369.75,
          "end": 372.18,
          "en": "is unconstrained horizontally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.18,
          "end": 374.58,
          "en": "there is a maximum width applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 374.58,
          "end": 377.67,
          "en": "by this row to this MealItemTrait here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.67,
          "end": 379.336,
          "en": "That's how this works here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.336,
          "end": 382.939,
          "en": "So that's the first piece of metadata being output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 382.939,
          "end": 387.03,
          "en": "Then I'll add a sized box here for some spacing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 387.03,
          "end": 389.883,
          "en": "with a width of let's say 12.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 391.02,
          "end": 392.19,
          "en": "And then the next MealItemTrait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.19,
          "end": 395.045,
          "en": "But here, I'm not outputting the duration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.045,
          "end": 397.233,
          "en": "but instead the complexity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 397.233,
          "end": 401.23,
          "en": "And I think here the work item is a good choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.23,
          "end": 406.17,
          "en": "Now, here I therefore want to output the complexity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 406.17,
          "end": 409.323,
          "en": "but the complexity is an enum.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 410.43,
          "end": 412.89,
          "en": "And if we take a look at the dummy data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 412.89,
          "end": 417.395,
          "en": "we see that it, for example, is a complexity of simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
